Test Requirements for Smart Event & Concert Ticket Booking Management System 

User Authentication & Profile Management:
The system shall allow a new customer or event organizer to register using a valid name, email, password, and user role. 
The system shall reject registration when the email format is invalid or required registration information is missing. 
The system shall allow a registered user to log in using valid credentials and issue an authorization token after successful authentication. 
The system shall deny access when invalid login credentials are entered. 
The system shall restrict functions according to the user's assigned role, including Buyer, Organizer, and Administrator. 

Event Search & Discovery 
The system shall allow users to browse available live events and concerts.
The system shall allow users to search for events using an event name or keyword. 
The system shall allow users to filter events by categories such as Concerts, Sports, and Theater.
The system shall display appropriate matching event information after a valid search or category selection.
The system shall display a suitable no-results message when no event matches the search criteria.

Event Organizer Management 
The system shall allow an authorized event organizer to create and publish event listings. 
The system shall allow the organizer to define event title, category, venue, date, ticket pricing, and seating information. 
The system shall allow the organizer to manage seating charts associated with an event. 
The system shall allow the organizer to view ticket sales information and analytics. 
The system shall prevent unauthorized users from accessing organizer management functions. 

Interactive Seat Selection & Booking
The system shall display the venue seating layout with real-time seat availability. 
The system shall visually identify Available, Locked/Reserved, and Sold seats. 
The system shall allow a logged-in customer to select one or more available seats. 
The system shall temporarily lock selected seats for 10 minutes during checkout. 
The system shall prevent another customer from booking a locked or sold seat. 
The system shall calculate and display the total order amount based on selected seats and ticket prices. 
The system shall release the temporary seat lock when payment fails or the lock period expires.

Promo Code & Checkout 
The system shall display an order summary and promo code field on the checkout screen.
The system shall accept a valid promotional code and apply the applicable discount. 
The system shall reject an invalid or expired promotional code without applying an incorrect discount.
The system shall display payment and order details before transaction submission. 
The system shall validate required checkout information before allowing payment. 

Payment Processing 
The system shall process ticket payments through the integrated third-party payment gateway. 
The system shall validate the payment response received from the external payment API.
The system shall display a success response when a valid payment transaction is completed.
The system shall display an appropriate failure response when payment is unsuccessful. 
The system shall handle payment timeout or gateway failure without creating an invalid confirmed booking.
The system shall release locked seats when payment fails.
The system shall maintain appropriate payment and transaction status information. 

Digital Ticket & QR Code Issuance 
The system shall generate a unique booking reference after successful payment. 
The system shall generate a downloadable PDF ticket after a confirmed booking.
The system shall generate and attach an encrypted QR code containing booking validation information. 
The system shall display the QR ticket to the customer after successful payment.
The system shall send the digital ticket or QR pass through the configured email service. 
The system shall not issue a confirmed QR ticket for an unsuccessful payment. 

Booking & Database Management 
The system shall store confirmed booking records with user, event, booking reference, total price, QR information, and timestamp. 
The system shall maintain unique identifiers for users, events, seats, and bookings. 
The system shall correctly update seat status from Available to Locked and then Sold after successful booking. 
The system shall maintain accurate seat inventory and prevent double-booking.
The system shall store event, seat, and booking information in the configured relational database. 

Security, Performance & Reliability 
The system shall transmit sensitive user information through encrypted HTTPS connections and protect stored passwords using bcrypt hashing. 
The system shall enforce role-based access control for Buyer, Organizer, and Administrator functions. 
The system shall support payment processing through the certified payment gateway according to the stated PCI-DSS requirement.
The system shall render seat selection updates within 1.5 seconds. 
The system shall support up to 2,000 concurrent booking requests. 
The system shall target 99.5% system availability and support daily database backup restoration. 
The system shall prevent double-booking during simultaneous attempts for the same seat. 

Administration & User Support 
The system shall allow an administrator to manage user accounts and oversee relevant system records. 
The system shall allow an administrator to manage posted content and review system logs. 
The system shall prevent Buyer and Organizer users from accessing administrator-only functions. 
The system shall provide an FAQ page for common user questions. 
The system shall provide an interactive online booking guide. 
